dered for conversion during the applicable make-whole conversion period will increase from 15.1763 shares to 16.2056 shares of common stock per $1,000 principal amount of notes, subject to further adjustment in accordance with the terms of the indenture. The Company elected to settle all conversions of the 2029 Convertible Notes in cash. In connection with the Redemption, the Company expects the capped call transactions entered into in connection with the issuance of the 2029 Convertible Notes to unwind and terminate in full. In connection with any such unwind and termination, the Company expects to receive from each option counterparty an amount of cash (or shares of the Company\u2019s common stock if agreed with the applicable option counterparty) reflecting the then-current option value of such capped call transaction. The Company expects to enter into bilateral unwind agreements with each option counterparty to unwind and terminate its respective capped call transaction as of or shortly following the Redemption Date. The Company\u2019s convertible\n"}
